<title>JAPAN: Japan 96/97 beef shipments fall by 7.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan 96/97 beef shipments fall by 7.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's beef shipments in the last fiscal year ended March fell by 7.3 percent from a year earlier to 990,324 tonnes, the Agriculture and Livestock Industries Corporation (ALIC) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The decline in shipments in 1996/97 was the first year-on-year fall since 1973/74. The ALIC said in a monthly report that the BSE (mad cow disease) scare and a nationwide bacterial outbreak were behind the lower beef shipments.</p>
<p>The industry body also said local beef output last fiscal year reached 382,668 tonnes, down by 7.5 percent from a year earlier. Beef imports fell by 7.2 percent to 611,241.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
